{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"negative exponent negative exponent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md","fileName":"Negative Exponent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Negative Exponent","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Exponents and Roots]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"negative exponent negative exponent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md","fileName":"Negative Exponent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Negative Exponent","heading":"Negative Exponent","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A negative exponent denotes the [[Reciprocal]] of the corresponding positive power. For nonzero (a),\n\n$$a^{-n}=\\frac{1}{a^n}.$$\n\nThis interpretation follows from (1=a^0=a^{n-n}=a^na^{-n}). It also means that taking a reciprocal reverses the sign of an exponent: (1/a^{-n}=a^n). Negative exponents do not make the value itself negative; for example, (2^{-3}=1/8). They describe position between numerator and denominator rather than arithmetic sign.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"negative exponent negative exponent","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Negative Exponent.md","fileName":"Negative Exponent.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Negative Exponent","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}